architecture itad-acquisition-desk
  canonical_name ITAD Acquisition Desk
  family surface
  domain Surface / Equipment inventory and acquisition decisions
  layer application
  semantic_question Which seller-described inventory, recovery assumptions, verification requirements and buyer inquiry belong to each equipment lot?
  purpose An acquisition workspace over the existing procurement-memory equipment contract with editable manifests, reviewed bulk changes, independent lot settings and exact-cent scenario comparisons
  maturity implemented
  source_path ../pages-procurement-memory/site/itad-exchange/core.mjs
  source_path ../pages-procurement-memory/site/itad-exchange/app.mjs
  source_path ../pages-procurement-memory/site/itad-exchange/manifest-grid.mjs
  source_path ../pages-procurement-memory/site/itad-exchange/index.html
  source_path ../pages-procurement-memory/site/itad-exchange/vendor/ag-grid-community-36.2.0/provenance.tsv
  source_path ../pages-procurement-memory/tests/itad-workspace.test.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/itad-desk-browser.mjs
  node_types EquipmentLot, ManifestLine, SellerClaim, RecoveryScenario, VerificationNeed, LocalRevision, BuyerInquiry
  internal_calculus manifest changes validate an immutable candidate against row, unit, identity and numeric bounds before replacing state; reviewed bulk proposals reject changes to their source generation
  internal_calculus resale sensitivity rounds each unit to cents before aggregation, reserve rounds upward, target proceeds round downward and the maximum unit bid floors the allowable acquisition amount divided by units
  internal_calculus version-one settings migrate legacy recipient, budget, mode and prepared status into independent lot snapshots; record-scoped undo retains other lots
  internal_calculus saves compare an expected workspace revision inside one existing IndexedDB transaction; in-flight save snapshots cannot absorb later edits
  invariant empty or partially unpriced inventory has no numeric net or maximum bid; zero recovery has no percentage margin
  invariant illustrative assumptions remain labeled through edits, imports, comparisons and exports; a manifest import cannot relabel retained illustrative acquisition costs as entered facts
  invariant new lots have no inventory or provider offers unless the caller explicitly chooses a template; the current new-lot interface does not choose one
  invariant pending form and grid edits retain unload protection; initial hydration blocks input, failed or stale saved-state reloads preserve the current draft
  invariant failed optional grid loading leaves a usable list editor over the same contract; retry retains its edits
  witness ../pages-procurement-memory/tests/itad-workspace.test.mjs checks atomic mutations, per-lot migration, custom lots, independently calculated integer-cent scenarios and provenance-bearing exports
  witness packs/no-simulation/product-maturity-20261015/itad/local/verification.json records 54 actual Chrome checks including grid edits, reviewed bulk changes, atomic import refusal, independent settings, revision conflicts, delayed-load guards and phone views
  witness packs/no-simulation/product-maturity-20261015/itad/live/verification.json repeats all 54 checks on the public preview without browser exceptions or remote writes
  witness packs/no-simulation/product-maturity-20261015/itad/deployment.json records preview e5f2d6ea-40f9-4086-9482-0e20ae6ab558 with unchanged Work Samples production
  forbidden_inference modeled profit, local review flags or a prepared inquiry -> independently verified inventory, accepted offer, buyer agreement, custody transfer or settlement
  forbidden_inference a browser-local workspace or preview deployment -> organization persistence, a changed GitHub Pages deployment or completion of the thirty-program scope
  known_gap sibling checkout owns the source; account and organization integration needs server authorization, native draft admission and a same-origin public transport
  known_gap full workspace backup, custom verification route editing, custody receipts, purchase execution and Google Stitch design generation remain open
